    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (74.01) standing as our premier offensive anchor. Facing Canning, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a strong SP Skill boost (+12%), positioning him to capitalize on a favorable matchup despite the park-adjusted drag. He is closely shadowed by **Sam Antonacci** (66.39), who leverages an elite leadoff spot (+10%) and an exceptional xwOBA projection of 0.400 against Miller. Meanwhile, **Josh Jung** (66.28) provides the day\u2019s most significant value-add; he faces the softest opposing arm in Peralta (5.12 xERA) and gains substantial momentum from a +19% SP skill advantage and a favorable park environment, making him a high-upside play at third base.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the fringe bench players, with **Nolan Schanuel** (51.09) landing just outside the starting nine. While **Nolan Schanuel** boasts decent efficiency against Lopez, the optimizer favored the higher-ceiling profiles of **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages** to maximize our output across the 5x5 categories. We continue to prioritize stolen base potential and lineup placement, which necessitated keeping **Nasim Nunez** (39.04) and **Coby Mayo** (34.00) on the bench. Both failed to clear the 40-point efficiency floor, largely due to unfavorable order positioning and the restrictive matchup against a high-skill arm like McLean. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the environment for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom draw tough assignments against Jax and McLean, respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** receives a slight efficiency bump (+2%) due to his ability to exploit slow SP deliveries for stolen bases, both players face negative park or SP skill modifiers that cap their upside. Ensure your lineups are finalized early; while **Jorge Polanco** remains on the IL, the rest of the active roster is set to provide the necessary speed and power metrics to keep the Waves competitive in our current 5x5 race.",
